{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Redone from the plan in worktree `cb1b-gate-async-starters` (the 2026-11-03 implementation never reached Gerrit or origin/main and its worktree is gone).\n\nPlan re-scoped after 2 BLOCK reviews, both verified against code: (1) `claim_ticket` and the `open -> in_progress` transition only run `claim_gate_check`, a local HMAC/freshness check with no LLM (`_commands/gates.py:319-366`), so `claim_ticket_start` was dropped; only the completion-gated close needs a starter. (2) No code-review path emits `sidecar_emitted`/`sidecar_reviewed_at`, so `_gate_sidecar_fields` stays unchanged. Third review: PASS, certified at b4e0d01b.\n\nImplemented: `review_code_start` (+ sync `review_code` on the same singleflight key), `transition_ticket_start` in new `_mcp_ticket_async.py` (gate type `transition`, verdict `applied`/failed-with-refusal), `gate_status` durable completion currency for transition jobs, generator + docs + AGENTS.md, golden/schema-coverage fixtures. Tests RED first (12 failing), now green; commit 2c507feb60e. `make verify` running."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1794858629356844714,"uuid":"79bceee9-b72a-43ae-9d45-d05628923217"}